            <div xml:id="d873">

                <pb facs="0746" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.931/4–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-30T17:00:00+08:00">April 30, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 30—5:30 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>908. KeDeptel 516, April 25. Communist soldiers were armed. Porter first sought
                    advice from Ambassador’s house boy [<hi rendition="#italic">chauffeur</hi>], but
                    on returning to gate was frightened to such extent by soldiers’ manner and
                    language as to unlock gate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
